# SPEC-071 R-3: per-turn model routing dev posture. Merged into the
# platform-runtime-config ConfigMap by the dev-k8s overlay; the code default
# keeps AGENTSCOPE_MODEL_ROUTER_ENABLED=false (deny-by-default), so an overlay
# that does not include this profile renders byte-identical to the router-off
# posture. This is the measurement-gated dev enablement R-3 deferred: the offline
# harness plus a live A/B/C run on a 24-turn sample reached 100% routing
# accuracy, so the router is switched on for the dev cluster here (scoped and
# reversible) rather than by flipping the shipped code default.
#
# The classifier (_MODEL) picks each reply's model over the candidate map by
# reading each candidate's description; candidates resolve against the
# credential-gated MODEL_CATALOG only, so an unknown/revoked id can never be
# routed to. This posture uses the always-keyed active provider (deepseek): a
# fast/cheap tier for routine turns and a high-capability tier for complex ones.
# Routing is fail-soft (a routing error or unknown candidate keeps the agent's
# own model) and resume-safe (the routed model survives a park/resume).
#
# NOTE: the classifier call is a separate ChatModelBase.generate_structured_output
# that does not ride SPEC-065 TokenUsageMiddleware, so its ~330-440 input +
# 10-34 output tokens/turn are not metered in agent_llm_tokens_total, and it adds
# ~0.5-0.8s latency per reply. Accepted for the dev cluster; revisit before any
# global default-on.
AGENTSCOPE_MODEL_ROUTER_ENABLED=true
AGENTSCOPE_MODEL_ROUTER_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash
AGENTSCOPE_MODEL_ROUTER_CANDIDATES={"fast":{"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","description":"Routine operator work: status checks, short factual lookups, simple summaries, and single-step questions where speed and low cost matter most."},"deep":{"model":"deepseek-v4-pro","description":"Complex work: multi-step reasoning, incident diagnosis and root-cause analysis, code or architecture review, planning, and nuanced judgment where capability matters most."}}
